# Windows launchers must be CRLF and pure ASCII.
#
# Why: cmd.exe parses batch files byte by byte. LF-only line endings plus
# non-ASCII text makes it misparse lines (half a line runs as a command,
# "pause" gets split), so the window flashes closed. That happened to people
# who downloaded the repo as a ZIP, where git serves the raw blobs.
#
# eol=crlf here fixes line endings on checkout and in `git archive`.
# Keeping the files ASCII (enforced by a test) is the real safety net: plain
# ASCII works even if LF somehow slips through.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf
